slug: writing-a-research-proposal
title: Writing a Research Proposal — Aims, Methods, Timeline and Budget
area: Research & Evidence
level: Clinical
best: Third year onwards
minutes: 12
hook: A proposal is a promise: "this is what I will do, how, when and with what". A clear one gets approved, funded and finished. A vague one gets sent back. Learn the parts, and learn to write each in plain, honest language. || Proposal ek waada hai: "main yeh karunga, kaise, kab aur kis ke saath". Saaf proposal manzoor, funded aur mukammal hota hai. Mubham wapas bheja jata hai. Hissay seekhein, aur har ek saade, imaandar alfaaz mein likhna seekhein.
goal: By the end, you'll structure a proposal (title, background, aims, methods, analysis, ethics, timeline, budget, references), write a clear methods section, build a realistic timeline and budget, and avoid the usual reasons proposals are rejected. || End tak aap proposal ka dhancha banayenge (title, background, aims, methods, analysis, ethics, timeline, budget, references), saaf methods section likhenge, haqeeqat pasand timeline aur budget banayenge, aur proposals ke radd hone ki aam wajuhaat se bachenge.
say: A good proposal answers eight questions: **Why** (background and gap), **What** (aims, hypothesis), **Who** (participants and eligibility), **How** (design, intervention, outcomes, sample size), **How will you analyse** it, **Is it ethical**, **When** (timeline) and **How much** (budget). Reviewers read many proposals quickly, so the first page must tell them what, why and how. Use the **SPIRIT** checklist for trial protocols. Write so that someone else could carry out your study from the document alone. || Achha proposal aath sawalon ka jawab deta hai: **Kyun** (background aur kami), **Kya** (aims, hypothesis), **Kaun** (shirkat karne wale aur eligibility), **Kaise** (design, intervention, nateeje, sample size), **tajziya kaise** hoga, **kya yeh akhlaqi hai**, **Kab** (timeline) aur **Kitna** (budget). Reviewers bohat se proposals jaldi parhte hain, isliye pehle safhe par kya, kyun aur kaise saaf hona chahiye. Trial protocols ke liye **SPIRIT** checklist istemal karein. Aise likhein ke koi doosra sirf dastavez se aap ka study chala sake.
analogy: Think of **a building plan and drawing**. An architect does not say "a nice house". They show the foundations, rooms, materials, schedule and cost, so a builder can build it and an owner can approve it. A proposal is the plan for a study, and if it is vague, the building will be too. || **Imarat ka naqsha aur drawing** sochein. Architect "achha ghar" nahi kehta. Woh bunyadein, kamray, saman, schedule aur kharch dikhata hai, taake builder bana sake aur malik manzoor kare. Proposal study ka naqsha hai, aur agar mubham ho to imarat bhi mubham hogi.
compare: Parts of a proposal and what to write || Proposal ke hissay aur kya likhein
head: Part || Hissa ;; What to write || Kya likhein ;; Typical length || Aam lambai
row: Title and summary || Title aur khulasa ;; A clear title and a 200-word summary with the question, method and expected value || Saaf title aur 200 alfaaz ka khulasa jis mein sawal, tareeqa aur mutawaqqe qeemat ho ;; One page || Ek safha
row: Background and rationale || Background aur wajah ;; What is known, what is not, and why this study is needed (cite recent reviews) || Kya maloom hai, kya nahi aur yeh study kyun zaroori hai (haal ke reviews ka hawala) ;; One to two pages || Ek se do safhay
row: Aims, objectives, hypothesis || Aims, objectives, hypothesis ;; One main aim, a few specific objectives and a testable hypothesis || Ek asal aim, chand khaas objectives aur aazmaye ja sakne wali hypothesis ;; Half a page || Aadha safha
row: Methods || Methods ;; Design, setting, participants, intervention, outcomes, sample size, procedures || Design, jagah, shirkat karne wale, intervention, nateeje, sample size, tareeqa-e-kaar ;; Two to four pages || Do se chaar safhay
row: Analysis, ethics, timeline, budget || Tajziya, ethics, timeline, budget ;; Planned statistics, consent and approval, a Gantt chart, itemised costs || Munsooba bandi shuda shumariyat, razamandi aur manzoori, Gantt chart, tafseeli kharch ;; One to two pages || Ek se do safhay
check: A reviewer reads "We will recruit patients with back pain and give them exercises." What is missing? || Reviewer parhta hai "Hum peeth dard ke mareezon ko bharti karenge aur unhein exercises denge." Kya kami hai?
ok: Details: who exactly (eligibility), what exercises, how long, compared with what, and how outcomes are measured || Tafseelat: bilkul kaun (eligibility), kaun si exercises, kitni der, kis se muqabla, aur nateeje kaise naape jayenge || Yes — a methods section must be specific enough to be repeated. || Haan — methods section itna khaas hona chahiye ke dohraya ja sake.
no: Nothing, it is clear enough || Kuch nahi, kaafi saaf hai || It is far too vague. || Yeh bohat mubham hai.
no: A longer title || Lamba title || The problem is detail, not the title. || Masla tafseel ka hai, title ka nahi.
check: Why is a Gantt chart useful in a proposal? || Proposal mein Gantt chart kyun mufeed hai?
ok: It shows each task on a timeline, so reviewers can see the study is realistic and you can track progress || Yeh har kaam ko timeline par dikhata hai, isliye reviewers dekh sakte hain ke study haqeeqat pasand hai aur aap pesh-raft track kar sakte hain || Yes — a good timeline builds confidence. || Haan — achhi timeline bharosa banati hai.
no: It lists the budget || Yeh budget ki list deta hai || The budget is separate. || Budget alag hai.
no: It replaces the methods section || Yeh methods section ki jagah leta hai || It supports it, not replaces. || Yeh madad karta hai, jagah nahi leta.
check: A student's budget lists "equipment: 200,000 rupees" with no detail. What should she do? || Ek talib-e-ilm ke budget mein "saman: 200,000 rupay" bina tafseel ke likha hai. Use kya karna chahiye?
ok: Itemise each cost with a reason and a quote, and include participant, staff and data-management costs || Har kharch ki wajah aur quote ke saath tafseel dein, aur shirkat karne wale, staff aur data-management ke kharch shamil karein || Yes — itemised costs show care and realism. || Haan — tafseeli kharch ehtiyat aur haqeeqat pasandi dikhate hain.
no: Keep it vague to give flexibility || Lachak ke liye mubham rakhe || Reviewers distrust vague budgets. || Reviewers mubham budget par shak karte hain.
no: Double it to be safe || Mehfooz rehne ke liye dugna kar de || Padded budgets are rejected. || Barhaye hue budget radd hote hain.
mistake: **Over-promising and under-planning.** "We will recruit 200 patients in three months" from a clinic that sees 10 a month is a fantasy. Reviewers prefer a modest, feasible plan with evidence (for example, last year's clinic numbers) to an ambitious one with no basis. Another trap is forgetting time for ethics approval, recruitment, data cleaning and writing, which usually take longer than you think. || **Zyada waade aur kam plan.** Ek clinic jo mahine mein 10 mareez dekhta ho woh "teen mahine mein 200 mareez bharti karenge" kahe to khayal-e-khaam hai. Reviewers haqeeqat pasand, saboot (masalan pichhle saal ke clinic numbers) wale saade plan ko bina bunyad ke ambitious plan par tarjeeh dete hain. Ek aur jaal ethics ki manzoori, bharti, data ki safai aur likhne ke liye waqt bhoolna hai, jo aam taur par socha se zyada lagta hai.
clinic: **Pilot your plan on a page.** Before you write the full proposal, draft a one-page outline and share it with a supervisor and a patient or colleague. Ask them to point to anything that is unclear or unrealistic. It is much cheaper to change a page than a protocol. Keep your first plan small enough to finish in 6 to 12 months. || **Pehle apne plan ka ek safha pilot karein.** Poora proposal likhne se pehle ek safha ka khaka likhein aur supervisor aur mareez ya saathi se share karein. Un se kahein har ghair-wazeh ya ghair-haqeeqi cheez par ungli rakhein. Safha badalna protocol badalne se bohat sasta hai. Apna pehla plan itna chhota rakhein ke 6 se 12 mahine mein mukammal ho.
reveal: Why do reviewers care so much about the outcome and the sample size? || Reviewers nateeje aur sample size ki itni parwah kyun karte hain? || Because they decide whether the study can answer the question. A vague outcome gives vague findings. An underpowered sample gives an inconclusive study, however well written. Reviewers also check that the primary outcome is chosen in advance (to avoid cherry-picking later) and that the sample size is based on a meaningful difference, with allowance for drop-outs. || Kyunke yeh tay karte hain ke study sawal ka jawab de sakti hai ya nahi. Mubham nateeja mubham findings deta hai. Underpowered sample ghair-faislakun study deta hai, chahe kitni achhi likhi ho. Reviewers yeh bhi dekhte hain ke primary outcome pehle se chuna gaya hai (baad mein chun-chun kar lene se bachne ke liye) aur sample size ba-maani farq par mabni hai, drop-outs ki gunjaish ke saath.
case: A therapist drafts a proposal for a pilot trial of a text-message reminder programme. The first draft says "patients will be contacted regularly", without a sample, a comparison or an outcome. || A reviewer asks: who, how often, compared with what, and how will success be measured? || She rewrites: 60 adults after knee replacement, weekly messages for 12 weeks compared with usual care, primary outcome exercise completion, with a 12-month Gantt chart and an itemised budget. || The revised proposal is approved, with a request to register the trial.
safety: **Plan for safety in the proposal.** Say how you will monitor and report adverse events, who will make stopping decisions and how participants can withdraw at any time without penalty. Include a plan for storing data securely. Reviewers and ethics committees look for these before anything else. || **Proposal mein safety ka plan shamil karein.** Batayein ke adverse events ki nigrani aur report kaise hogi, rokne ka faisla kaun karega aur shirkat karne wale kisi bhi waqt bina saza ke kaise wapas ja sakte hain. Data mehfooz rakhne ka plan shamil karein. Reviewers aur ethics committees sab se pehle yehi dekhte hain.
evidence: The SPIRIT 2013 statement defines a checklist of 33 items that a clinical trial protocol should address, including administrative information, introduction, methods (participants, interventions, outcomes, sample size, recruitment, data collection and analysis), ethics and dissemination. Its aim is to improve the completeness and transparency of protocols, which are the plans that reviewers, ethics committees and later readers use to judge a study. || SPIRIT 2013 statement 33 items ki checklist tay karta hai jin ka clinical trial protocol ko hal dena chahiye, jis mein intizami maloomat, introduction, methods (shirkat karne wale, interventions, nateeje, sample size, bharti, data jama karna aur tajziya), ethics aur isha'at shamil hain. Is ka maqsad protocols ki mukammaliat aur shaffafiyat behtar karna hai, jo woh plans hain jin se reviewers, ethics committees aur baad ke parhne walay study ko parakhte hain.
memory: **Why, What, Who, How, When, How much.** The six questions every proposal must answer clearly. || **Kyun, Kya, Kaun, Kaise, Kab, Kitna.** Chhe sawal jin ka har proposal ko saaf jawab dena hai.
summary: A proposal answers why, what, who, how, analysis, ethics, when and how much. || Proposal kyun, kya, kaun, kaise, tajziya, ethics, kab aur kitna ka jawab deta hai.
summary: Write methods specifically enough to repeat, and use a Gantt chart and itemised budget. || Methods itne khaas likhein ke dohraye ja sakein, aur Gantt chart aur tafseeli budget istemal karein.
summary: Be realistic and modest, plan for safety and use SPIRIT for trial protocols. || Haqeeqat pasand aur saade rahein, safety ka plan banayein aur trial protocols ke liye SPIRIT istemal karein.
card: What is a Gantt chart? || Gantt chart kya hai? || A timeline chart showing each task and its dates. || Timeline chart jo har kaam aur uski tareekhein dikhata hai.
card: What does SPIRIT guide? || SPIRIT kis ki rehnumai karta hai? || The content of clinical trial protocols. || Clinical trial protocols ka mawad.
card: Why itemise a budget? || Budget ki tafseel kyun dein? || It shows care and realism and builds reviewer trust. || Yeh ehtiyat aur haqeeqat pasandi dikhata hai aur reviewer ka bharosa banata hai.
card: What should the first page of a proposal tell a reviewer? || Proposal ka pehla safha reviewer ko kya batana chahiye? || What you will do, why it matters and how. || Aap kya karenge, kyun ahem hai aur kaise.
deeper: Choosing a research question (FINER) || /learn/choosing-a-research-question-finer || The question behind the proposal. || Proposal ke peechay ka sawal.
deeper: Sample size and power || /learn/sample-size-and-power-intuition || The numbers in the methods. || Methods ke numbers.
source: Chan AW, Tetzlaff JM, Altman DG, et al. SPIRIT 2013 statement: defining standard protocol items for clinical trials. Ann Intern Med 2013;158:200-207. || SPIRIT 2013 statement defining standard protocol items for clinical trials Chan
source: Hulley SB, Cummings SR, Browner WS, Grady DG, Newman TB. Designing clinical research. 4th ed. Philadelphia: Lippincott Williams and Wilkins; 2013. || Designing clinical research Hulley Cummings Browner
